  "equipment_type": "Make-up air unit controls (discharge temperature and humidity)",
  "applies_to": "AbsolutAire units with the PC-3 (LC-3) psychrometric control package for discharge temperature, dehumidification, humidification and optional airflow control.",
  "summary": "The PC-3 user guide covers AbsolutAire's psychrometric controls package (the preface calls it LC-3), which holds discharge temperature and humidity by cooling to a dew point and reheating, with optional humidification and VFD airflow control. The controller joins a BACnet MS/TP network, finds the baud rate itself and takes its MAC address from DIP switches. The BMS can switch the unit on and off and write discharge temperature, humidity and airflow setpoints.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "3640 followed by the MAC address (MAC 25 = 364025)",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The guide prints 'degrees-Fahrenheit' as the unit for humidity, airflow and command-percent points; those units are corrected here (%RH, CFM, %).",
    "MV 25 and MV 27 repeat the descriptions of MV 24 and MV 26 in the guide; by name they are the return temperature and return humidity sensor alarms.",
    "Multistate alarm objects use AbsolutAire enumerations named in the guide (Filters, Alarm / Normal, Lockout / Normal, SensorReliability) without listing the state numbers.",
    "The ControlType BV is printed as Boolean (SPACE;DISCHARGE) without saying which state is 1.",
    "Names are kept as printed, including typos (HumiditficationCommand, network_MazimumEconomizer_VFD, DirtyPreFitlerAlarm)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "PC-3 User Guide - Network Integration",
    "doc_number": "PC-3 User Guide 010220",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.absolutaire.com/wp-content/uploads/pc_3_users_guide.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set the MAC address on the DIP switches and connect to the BACnet MS/TP trunk; the controller detects the baud rate after a power cycle and its device instance becomes 3640 followed by the MAC. Command the unit with network_FanCommand and write the discharge temperature and humidity setpoints; read the discharge conditions, command outputs and the multistate alarms.",
